You are deciding whether one evidence bucket represents a single coherent experimental readout.

A coherent readout is a set of observations that measure the same quantity or outcome with the same scientific interpretation. Consider differences in endpoint, unit or scale, measured transporter, assay system, species, and kinetic quantity only when they change what was actually measured. Ignore downstream predictive usefulness, record count, repetition, and wording differences.

If the bucket is coherent, return COHERENT. If it contains more than one intrinsic readout, return SPLIT and select the single supplied unused canonical column that best separates those readouts.

